Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.12,0:00:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Physics hands the machine\Ntwo kinds of laws.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.31,0:00:08.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Some hold for every single snapshot.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.92,0:00:11.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Others hold only for the crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.17,0:00:13.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Two shelves, still empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.88,0:00:18.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Back to the three dials, at a\N{\c&H7AAF1B&}Gamma{\c&HF7F4F2&} never seen in training.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.34,0:00:19.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Grey: true snapshots.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.93,0:00:21.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Violet: a plain {\c&HF09CB4&}generator{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.90,0:00:23.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The shape is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.24,0:00:25.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now weigh the sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.78,0:00:28.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The truth is balanced; the machine is not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.02,0:00:32.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Only about four in ten of\Nits snapshots point up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.80,0:00:35.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It copied its data: below the threshold,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.80,0:00:40.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}each run stays in one whirlpool,\Nand the runs split unevenly.
